<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA-INDIA THIRD DAY SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA-INDIA THIRD DAY SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>DURBAN, South Africa 1996-12-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard on the</p>
<p>third day of the first cricket test between India and South</p>
<p>Africa at Kingsmead on Saturday:</p>
<p>South Africa first innings 235 (A.Hudson 80; V.Prasad 5-60)</p>
<p>India first innings 100 (A.Donald 5-40)</p>
<p>South Africa second innings (overnight 164 for four)</p>
<p> A.Hudson c Tendulkar b Kumble			52</p>
<p> G.Kirsten c Dravid b Prasad			   2</p>
<p> A.Bacher c Tendulkar b Kumble			55</p>
<p> D.Cullinan c Mongia b Prasad			  3</p>
<p> H.Cronje c Mongia b Prasad			   17</p>
<p> H.Gibbs lbw b Srinath				  25</p>
<p> B.McMillan not out				     51</p>
<p> S.Pollock c Rathore b Prasad			  2</p>
<p> D.Richardson b Srinath				  4</p>
<p> L.Klusener c Mongia b Srinath			 4</p>
<p> A.Donald c Rathore b Prasad			  26</p>
<p> Extras (b-7 lb-6 nb-5)				 18</p>
<p> Total (all out in 71 overs)			 259</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-4 2-115 3-120 4-120 5-164 6-164 7-171 8-181</p>
<p>9-185.</p>
<p>Bowling: Srinath 23-5-80-3 (1-nb), Prasad 25-4-93-5 (2-nb),</p>
<p>Johnson 9-1-39-0 (2-nb), Kumble 11-3-26-2, Ganguly 2-0-8-0.</p>
<p>	 India second innings</p>
<p>    V.Rathore c Richardson b Donald		   2</p>
<p>    W.Raman b Donald					1</p>
<p>    S.Ganguly b Donald				    0</p>
<p>    S.Tendulkar c Kirsten b Pollock		   4</p>
<p>    M.Azharuddin c Klusener b Pollock		 8</p>
<p>    R.Dravid not out				     27</p>
<p>    N.Mongia c Cronje b Kumble			  4</p>
<p>    A.Kumble c Hudson b Klusener			2</p>
<p>    J.Srinath run out				     7</p>
<p>    D.Johnson c Klusener b Pollock		    5</p>
<p>    V.Prasad c Hudson b Donald			  1</p>
<p>    Extras (lb-2 nb-3)				    5</p>
<p>    Total (all out in 34.1 overs)		    66</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-2 2-2 3-7 4-15 5-20 6-25 7-40 8-51 9-59.</p>
<p>Bowling: Donald 11.1-4-14-4, Pollock 12-4-25-3 (1-nb),</p>
<p>Klusener 9-2-16-2 (2-nb), McMillan 2-0-9-0.</p>
<p>Result: South Africa won by 328 runs.</p>
<p>The second test is at Newlands from January 2-6 and the</p>
<p>third and final test at the Wanderers from January 16-20.</p>
